// demand_vs_capacity.kql
// Feeds Activator rule RULE-DEMAND-90: "Demand exceeds 90% of available
// capacity". Also answers the canned Copilot question:
//   "Available peaker headroom vs reserve margin" (see peaker_headroom
//   section below).
//
// NATIVE scoring: calls AvailableCapacityNow() defined in
// phase3_native_scoring.kql, which computes available capacity live from
// ERP nameplate data joined with the current on/offline status of every
// generator -- no externally pre-computed grid_summary required.

AvailableCapacityNow()
| where demand_pct_of_capacity > 90.0

// ---------- peaker headroom (Copilot question) ----------
PeakerHeadroomNow()
